wayland: present software window surfaces through wl_shm

The Wayland backend has no window framebuffer, so SDL_GetWindowSurface()
always goes through the GPU texture framebuffer. Without a GPU, that is
llvmpipe: the whole GL stack loaded, and a full-screen texture upload
and draw for every SDL_UpdateWindowSurface() where a memory copy would
do.

Add one: a small set of wl_shm buffers committed to the window's surface
in turn. A buffer is not written again until the compositor releases it.
When none is free another is allocated, and only once there are four
does an update wait for a release. Damage comes from the update rects,
and a resize makes a new framebuffer.

By default the window surface is memory of its own and an update copies
the updated area into a free buffer, so its contents persist as they do
on other backends. SDL_HINT_VIDEO_WAYLAND_FRAMEBUFFER_NO_COPY makes the
window surface's pixels the buffers themselves: an update presents them
and points the surface at the next free buffer, for applications that
redraw every pixel each frame anyway.

The framebuffer is XRGB8888 unless SDL_HINT_VIDEO_WAYLAND_SHM_FORMAT
asks for one of the 24-bit formats and wl_shm offers it, so wl_shm's
formats are now recorded as the compositor advertises them. 24-bit rows
are padded to a multiple of 12 bytes: wl_shm needs a multiple of 3 and
pixman one of 4.

The texture framebuffer is still used first unless
SDL_HINT_FRAMEBUFFER_ACCELERATION turns it off.

Signed-off-by: badgeos
---
diff --git a/include/SDL3/SDL_hints.h b/include/SDL3/SDL_hints.h
index ba2ff35..e7b4f73 100644
--- a/include/SDL3/SDL_hints.h
+++ b/include/SDL3/SDL_hints.h
@@ -3921,6 +3921,34 @@ extern "C" {
  */
 #define SDL_HINT_VIDEO_WAYLAND_ALLOW_LIBDECOR "SDL_VIDEO_WAYLAND_ALLOW_LIBDECOR"
 
+/**
+ * A variable controlling whether the Wayland window framebuffer is presented
+ * without a copy.
+ *
+ * By default, the window surface returned by SDL_GetWindowSurface() keeps its
+ * contents across updates: SDL_UpdateWindowSurface() copies the updated area
+ * into a buffer the compositor has released and presents that. With this
+ * hint enabled, the window surface's pixels are themselves a buffer shared
+ * with the compositor. An update presents them as they are and points the
+ * surface's `pixels` at another released buffer, whose contents are
+ * undefined. The application must then redraw the whole surface after every
+ * update, reading `pixels` again, or call SDL_GetWindowSurface() each frame.
+ *
+ * This applies to the Wayland window framebuffer only, which is used when
+ * SDL_HINT_FRAMEBUFFER_ACCELERATION disables the texture framebuffer.
+ *
+ * The variable can be set to the following values:
+ *
+ * - "0": Updates copy the window surface; its contents persist. (default)
+ * - "1": Updates present the window surface without a copy; its contents are
+ *   undefined afterward.
+ *
+ * This hint should be set before calling SDL_GetWindowSurface().
+ *
+ * \since This hint is available since SDL 3.4.10.
+ */
+#define SDL_HINT_VIDEO_WAYLAND_FRAMEBUFFER_NO_COPY "SDL_VIDEO_WAYLAND_FRAMEBUFFER_NO_COPY"
+
 /**
  * A variable controlling whether video mode emulation is enabled under
  * Wayland.
@@ -4022,6 +4050,33 @@ extern "C" {
  */
 #define SDL_HINT_VIDEO_WAYLAND_SCALE_TO_DISPLAY "SDL_VIDEO_WAYLAND_SCALE_TO_DISPLAY"
 
+/**
+ * A variable specifying the pixel format of the Wayland window framebuffer.
+ *
+ * The window surface returned by SDL_GetWindowSurface() uses this format if
+ * the compositor's wl_shm supports it, and the default otherwise. A 24-bit
+ * format saves the compositor a conversion on a display that scans out
+ * 24-bit pixels.
+ *
+ * This applies to the Wayland window framebuffer only, which is used when
+ * SDL_HINT_FRAMEBUFFER_ACCELERATION disables the texture framebuffer.
+ *
+ * The variable can be set to one of the following pixel format names, as
+ * SDL_GetPixelFormatName() returns them:
+ *
+ * - "SDL_PIXELFORMAT_XRGB8888": 32 bits per pixel, WL_SHM_FORMAT_XRGB8888.
+ *   (default)
+ * - "SDL_PIXELFORMAT_BGR24": 24 bits per pixel, B, G, R in memory,
+ *   WL_SHM_FORMAT_RGB888.
+ * - "SDL_PIXELFORMAT_RGB24": 24 bits per pixel, R, G, B in memory,
+ *   WL_SHM_FORMAT_BGR888.
+ *
+ * This hint should be set before calling SDL_GetWindowSurface().
+ *
+ * \since This hint is available since SDL 3.4.10.
+ */
+#define SDL_HINT_VIDEO_WAYLAND_SHM_FORMAT "SDL_VIDEO_WAYLAND_SHM_FORMAT"
+
 /**
  * A variable specifying which shader compiler to preload when using the
  * Chrome ANGLE binaries.
diff --git a/src/video/wayland/SDL_waylandframebuffer.c b/src/video/wayland/SDL_waylandframebuffer.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b694e7a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/video/wayland/SDL_waylandframebuffer.c
@@ -0,0 +1,480 @@
+/*
